From f3d1aa38239e29763997c07a16c04258b3c9f648 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:42:08 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op menu: the Insert menu takes the pads the game would,
 whichever window is in front

Patch 0037 let the co-op module open Longshot's own menu with no key (HOS_COOP_MENU_WANT_LONGSHOT), so the pause menu's Longshot Settings works with the game's window behind. The menu then took no input: vk_menu.cpp read the pads only while the game's window was the foreground one (mine && host->pad_raw), while host/nn_hid.c, behind other windows with Controller in background or a picked pad, gave those pads to the game even with the menu open. The pad's B closed the game's pause under the menu.

nn_hid.c: one pad path in front and behind (pads_to_game): while the menu is open the pads are its own and each waits until let go after it closes; behind with the pads not the game's, pad_raw_now is 0. A test's presses (HOS_INPUT_SCRIPT, the control bridge) while the menu is open are the menu's too, as the pad inputs bound to them, and kept from the game (test_presses_to_menu). hos_pad_raw gives both.
vk_menu.cpp: the pads with no focus test of the menu's (the host decides); Restart/Quit's second press and the Controls page's confirmation take the player's pad behind other windows (mine || pad_last).
(Longshot's tests/ is not in the Linux AppImage the kit patches: the behaviour test is oot-remake-multiplayer's tools/hookshot/menu_pads_behind_test.py, on the patched source. tests/test_pads_after_menu.py, test_input_background.py and test_menu_text_field.py still cut the old blocks.)
